                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j \geq \alpha
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is Cauchy if and only if it equivalent to itself, and it is easy to prove that two Cauchy sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
