          %p
            In this sense, the Dedekind real numbers is the collection of
            %em all
            real numbers.
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in F
            is a
            %strong Cauchy real number
            if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} there exists
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locator"} locator
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %strong Cauchy real numbers
            are the set of Dedekind real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
